      "title": "Start here",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "# Clip from Premiere -- no export, no re-encode\n\n**Needs the ComfyUI Bridge panel running in Premiere.**\n\nIn Premiere, select a clip -- in the timeline or in the project panel -- then click **Clip -> ComfyUI** in the panel. Three things fill in on the node below: the clip's file path, and its in and out points in seconds. Then the workflow runs itself.\n\nNothing gets exported and nothing gets rendered. The panel simply tells ComfyUI where the footage already lives on disk, and ComfyUI opens it directly.\n\n**Success looks like:** the same clip turning up in your `ComfyUI Results` bin, plus a frame count in the preview box. Nothing has been changed yet -- that's the point. It's the smallest possible proof the wiring works, before you put real work in the middle."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
