      "title": "Two ways out of one node",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## Two ways out of one node\n\n**Clip from Premiere** hands you the same clip twice over, and which one you use depends on what you're doing.\n\n**segments** is the metadata list -- the exact same shape the Load Premiere Timeline nodes produce. So everything in `01_read_a_premiere_edit.json` works here too, only on a live selection instead of an exported file. Here it feeds Get Premiere Segment, which reports the clip's frame count.\n\n**video** is a ready-to-use VIDEO. Feed it a video model, a Save Video node, or send it straight back to Premiere as it is.\n\n`start_seconds` and `end_seconds` sitting at `0.0` mean \"the whole clip\". The panel fills them in for you when the thing you selected is trimmed.\n\n**To make this do something:** put a video workflow between the two nodes on the right, and change `label` so you can tell the result apart from the source.\n\nThe other outputs -- `path`, `start_seconds`, `end_seconds` -- come back out so you can pass them to nodes that want a filename or a time range."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
